bunch [[Cookbook:Oregano|oregano]]\n* ½ bunch flat-leaf [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]]\n* 2 sprigs [[Cookbook:Rosemary|rosemary]]\n* ½ bunch [[Cookbook:Thyme|thyme]]\n* Several thin slices of red [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 6 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], smashed\n* Several thin slices of [[Cookbook:Lemon|lemon]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* [[Cookbook:Pepper|Black pepper]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] white [[Cookbook:Wine|wine]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Seafood|seafood]] [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Coat fish with olive oil, then sprinkle liberally with salt and freshly-ground black pepper, inside and out.\n#Stuff cavity with herbs, garlic, onion, and lemon. Score skin in a diamond pattern.\n#Combine seafood stock and white wine in a gallon size zip-top plastic bag. Insert fish, remove as much air as possible, and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes.\n#[[Cookbook:Grilling|Grill]] over medium high heat for 6–8 minutes per side. Remove and rest for 7 minutes. Serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using fish]]\n[[Category:Marinade recipes]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dill]]\n[[Category:Recipes using seafood broth and stock]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Herb Grilled Snapper","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 ea. (2 lb) whole red snapper, cleaned, fins removed and head and tail left intact","sourceText":"1 ea. (2 lb) whole red snapper, cleaned, fins removed and head and tail left intact","amountText":"1 ea. (2 lb) whole red snapper, cleaned, fins removed and head and tail left intact","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Olive oil","sourceText":"Olive oil","amountText":"Olive oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"½ bunch dill","sourceText":"½ bunch dill","amountText":"½ bunch dill","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBin